    "name": "Desert Trails Iris Rhizome",
    "description": "<p dir=\"ltr\"><span style=\"white-space: pre-wrap;\">\"Desert Trails\" is a&nbsp;Tall Bearded Iris&nbsp;(TB) introduced by Keith Keppel in 2017. It's known for its unique plicata pattern, featuring colonial buff standards with a lighter marguerite yellow center, pale dove grey dots, and citron yellow falls with a dark greyed purple edge and haft.&nbsp;The beards are white with bronzed yellow tips, and the style arms are quince yellow</span></p>",
